                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0c23ee5d-9385-32d9-acdb-c8a0afc7b2a1",
                        "entry_id": "69684fb6-e11f-3d5c-a3a6-bb7712cecef5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To be without, or to resign, possession of."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2cf06f4b-9756-4054-83c6-f9d82a6b1b97",
                                "sense_id": "0c23ee5d-9385-32d9-acdb-c8a0afc7b2a1",
                                "text": "This is a farce. Since when did I receive the gun (which is possessing it) and then unpossess it, and, then possess it again (all from 1984 to 1985) ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a764b424-4c4a-4919-848b-fa016b5540f2",
                                "sense_id": "0c23ee5d-9385-32d9-acdb-c8a0afc7b2a1",
                                "text": "Users can select whether the Soul should continue to refer to the original Body (B_C on the host A) or it should unpossess the old Body and possess a one on the host B."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a201e46-f6c8-4723-b235-64f1f98872ac",
                                "sense_id": "0c23ee5d-9385-32d9-acdb-c8a0afc7b2a1",
                                "text": "These two events are called when this player controller possesses and unpossesses a pawn."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "21355ec1-585a-3257-adec-06324d66dd41",
                        "entry_id": "69684fb6-e11f-3d5c-a3a6-bb7712cecef5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To free from an obsession that has taken hold of (someone)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e4826a3-9cb7-4bc4-94c9-9d8a0bd97722",
                                "sense_id": "21355ec1-585a-3257-adec-06324d66dd41",
                                "text": "The hold that is given over I unpossess, so hangeth now in balance Of war my peace, reward of all my pain, At Mountzon thus I restless rest in Spain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "68fda490-c3ac-44ee-a54c-1ea36f8ef830",
                                "sense_id": "21355ec1-585a-3257-adec-06324d66dd41",
                                "text": "[…] but she also exits as a new person, for to be free, she had to unpossess herself of her \"possession,\" her passion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4edb7ccd-ef72-4da2-9d35-eba846f13760",
                                "sense_id": "21355ec1-585a-3257-adec-06324d66dd41",
                                "text": "She was posssessed, Nausicaa was, and no amount of reminding her of Odysseus's age and marital status could unpossess her ."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
